{
  "$comment": [
    "AUTHORITATIVE SEED CONTRACT for the Meridian Launch Systems demo data plane.",
    "",
    "One file, three consumers:",
    "  1. data/seed/sql/*.sql        - the T-SQL DDL is written to match this exactly.",
    "  2. data/seed/seed.ps1         - load order, row-count assertions, column order.",
    "  3. data/seed/tests/*.Tests.ps1 - parity tests compare this to BOTH the DDL and the",
    "                                   generator source (data/generators/build.py, pools.py).",
    "",
    "Column names and their ORDER are the same order data/generators/writers.py emits",
    "(dict insertion order == CSV header order == JSON key order). Do not reorder.",
    "",
    "planes:",
    "  operational       - Azure SQL is the system of record; launch-ops (L7) does CRUD here.",
    "  reference         - seeded once, read-mostly, FK targets for the operational tables.",
    "  analytical-mirror - the LAKEHOUSE is the system of record (master plan L5/L6: the",
    "                      Cost Management Function writes cost_daily into mls_operations);",
    "                      the Azure SQL copy exists so L7 app views can join without",
    "                      crossing planes, and is refreshed by re-seeding, never by app writes.",
    "",
    "sql_type is the Azure SQL column type. Rule: FLOAT for every non-currency real number",
    "(IEEE double - round-trips a Python float exactly and cannot overflow), DECIMAL(18,2)",
    "for currency, INT for counters/years, DATE for ISO YYYY-MM-DD, BIT for booleans,",
    "NVARCHAR sized at roughly 2-4x the widest value the seed actually produces.",
    "",
    "spark_type is NOT used by the default lakehouse loader (the Load Table REST API cannot",
    "accept a schema - see data/seed/lakehouse/README.md). It is carried so the documented",
    "notebook upgrade path is mechanical rather than a re-derivation."
  ],
  "generator_seed": 20260822,
